  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 130 AM Thursday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Showers and thunderstorms will be on the increase \nagain, especially Sunday into next week. Temperatures continue to be \nnear average. \n\nHigh pressure will shift from the Upper Mississippi Valley to over \nthe Mid-Atlantic states Friday, then offshore Saturday. Temperatures \nwill continue to be near normal on Saturday, with only a slight \nchance of a PM thunderstorm in the west. Lows in the upper 60s to \nlower 70s and highs in the upper 80s to lower 90s. \n\nThere is expected to be the development of a mid/upper trough over \nthe Tennessee/Ohio Valley regions Sunday into Monday, then linger \ninto mid-week. Expect rapidly increasing moisture with showers and \nthunderstorms expected again Sunday into next week with a deep \nsoutherly flow expected.  \n\nAdditional heavy rainfall is possible late in the weekend into next \nweek that may continue to bring big relief with the ongoing drought. \n\nThe return of moisture with a trough likely developing just west of \nthe Appalachians will keep the temperatures check Sunday into early \nnext week. Highs should hold in the lower to mid 80s.",
